---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Carousel } from "../components/Carousel";
import Event from "../components/Event.astro";
---

<Layout title="Gordon Lockwood">
  <section class="relative">
    <img src="/images/graphic.webp" alt="" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl" />
    <h1
      class="font-display absolute bottom-2 w-full text-center text-3xl tracking-tight text-blue-800 uppercase [word-spacing:1rem] sm:bottom-10 sm:text-4xl md:bottom-16 md:text-5xl lg:bottom-20 lg:text-6xl"
      style="text-shadow: 1px 1px currentColor;"
    >
      Gordon Lockwood
    </h1>
  </section>

  <p class="mx-auto mb-20 max-w-prose text-center text-lg md:text-xl">
    Jeremiah Lockwood and Ricky Gordon have been making music together for over
    two decades, originally as disciples of Piedmont Blues legend Carolina Slim.
    For their first post-pandemic live shows they have begun a new duo to share
    the sonic pleasures stored up over a tumultuous year of longing. Expect old
    time blues, new-time rhythms, and ballads about all the things we want to do
    with you.
  </p>

  <a
    href="https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/CTV/2025/07/07/r-b-duo-gordon-lockwood-talks-summer-concert-series"
    target="_blank"
    class="mx-auto mb-20 block max-w-prose text-center text-lg md:text-xl"
  >
    <figure>
      <img src="/images/NY1.png" alt="NY1 thumbnail" class="mx-auto w-lg" />
      <figcaption class="font-bold text-blue-800 underline">
        Watch the NY1 news clip
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </a>

  <section id="media">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
      <Carousel
        client:load
        videos={[
          { id: "dLHMwI10Dwo", width: 560, height: 315 },
          { id: "0uHk1MXrhGw", width: 560, height: 315 }, // Meet Me In the Bottom
          { id: "wgrvYu4QGpA", width: 560, height: 315 }, // Once Upon a Time the Fire Burned Brighter
          { id: "j92oXP9pWbA", width: 560, height: 315 }, // Snap Your Fingers
          { id: "WB0VMW2ACiE", width: 560, height: 315 }, // Big Leg Woman
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2 class="my-10 text-center text-2xl font-bold">Upcoming events</h2>

  <section id="events" class="mb-20">
    <div
      class="mx-auto max-w-4xl overflow-x-scroll border-4 border-dashed border-indigo-400 p-2"
    >
      <div class="flex w-max gap-2 bg-indigo-300">
        <Event
          title="Gordon Lockwood - July Residency at Barbès"
          date="July 5, 12, 19, 26 at 6pm"
          address="376 9th Street, Park Slope, Brooklyn"
          description={["https://www.barbesbrooklyn.com/"]}
        />
        <Event
          title="Gordon Lockwood at Blues by the Boardwalk - Pier 97"
          address="Hudson River Park (at 57th St on the river)"
          date="Tuesday, August 5 6:30pm"
          description={[]}
        />
        <Event
          title="Gordon Lockwood at Terra Blues"
          date="Thursday, August 21 7-9:30pm"
          address="149 Bleecker Street, Manhattan"
          description={["https://www.terrablues.com/"]}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2 class="my-10 text-center text-2xl font-bold">About the artists</h2>
  <section id="about" class="mx-auto mb-20 max-w-4xl text-center">
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-10 lg:flex-row">
      <div class="text-xl">
        <h3 class="font-bold">Jeremiah Lockwood</h3>
        <p class="max-w-prose">
          Singer/guitarist Jeremiah Lockwood is the founder of The Sway
          Machinery, a world-exploring, genre-defying band perhaps best known
          for its collaborations with the late great Khaira Arby of Timbuktu.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img
        src="/images/lockwood.jpg"
        width="580"
        height="320"
        alt="Jeremiah Lockwood"
        class="border-4 border-dashed border-indigo-400 p-2"
      />
    </div>
    <div
      class="mt-10 flex flex-col items-center gap-10 text-center lg:flex-row-reverse"
    >
      <div class="text-xl">
        <h3 class="font-bold">Ricky "Dirty Red" Gordon</h3>
        <p class="max-w-prose">
          Drummer Ricky Gordon is a member of the Wynton Marsalis Ensemble and a
          prolific composer for the screen, including iconic collaborations with
          Spike Lee.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img
        src="/images/gordon.jpg"
        width="500"
        height="333"
        alt='Ricky "Dirty Red" Gordon'
        class="border-4 border-dashed border-indigo-400 p-2"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside id="album-notice" class="mx-auto mt-40 text-lg">
    <a
      href="https://ayinpress.org/folio/once-upon-a-time-the-fire-burned-brighter/"
      target="_blank"
      class="block w-full"
    >
      <figure>
        <img
          src="/images/once_upon_a_time_the_fire_burned_brighter.png"
          alt="Once Upon A Time The Fire Burned Brighter"
          class="w-full"
        />
        <figcaption class="text-center text-xl">
          Debut EP from Gordon Lockwood!!
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </a>
    <div
      class="mx-auto my-10 flex w-full max-w-max flex-col gap-10 lg:flex-row"
    >
      <p class="max-w-prose">
        In the multimedia album <cite>
          Once Upon a Time the Fire Burned Brighter: Ballads from the Yiddish
          Gothic</cite
        >, scholar and musician Jeremiah Lockwood opens a doorway into the rich
        sensorium of the Yiddish ballad. Drawing deeply from the work of
        legendary Yiddish folk singer Lifshe Schaechter-Widman, the collection
        reimagines and recasts Yiddish ballads through audio and video
        performances by Gordon Lockwood (the musical project of Lockwood and
        drummer Ricky Gordon), which appear beside archival visuals, lyric
        adaptations, and textual explorations. Once Upon a Time the Fire Burned
        Brighter invites us to experience a body of Jewish song that emerges
        from a world of fantasy, memory, and symbol—constituting a Yiddish
        gothic, a folk expressionism unapologetic in the extremes of its
        enticing imagery.
      </p>
      <div class="mx-auto flex w-max flex-col gap-5">
        <a
          href="https://ayinpress.org/folio/once-upon-a-time-the-fire-burned-brighter/"
          target="_blank"
          class="text-center underline"
        >
          Read more
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://open.spotify.com/album/25xbK0u9KQZduumUkw1ynM?si=E5DzlbeyTdG6wQFPIfzmiQ"
          target="_blank"
          class="flex w-max items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-black px-2 py-1 text-indigo-50"
        >
          Listen on <img
            src="/images/spotify.svg"
            alt="Spotify"
            class="inline-block w-20"
          />
        </a>
        <a
          <a
          href="https://music.apple.com/us/album/once-upon-a-time-the-fire-burned-brighter-ballads/1674810118"
          target="_blank"
          class="flex w-max items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-gradient-to-b from-indigo-600 to-sky-600 px-2 py-1 text-indigo-50"
        >
          Listen on <img
            src="/images/apple-music.svg"
            alt="Apple Music"
            class="inline-block w-20"
          />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </aside>
</Layout>
